WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.065 --> 00:00:00.690
YUFENG GUO: Hi.

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:01.920
My name is Yufeng Guo.

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:03.690
And today we're
going to explore how

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:06.210
you can build a solution
with Google Cloud AI

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:09.780
by taking a look at the use case
of using AI in manufacturing

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:11.610
for increased productivity.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:14.290
Our example comes from
the machining industry.

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:17.730
So let's first talk a bit
about what machining is.

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:19.410
Machining is the
process for cutting

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:21.600
raw materials, such
as metal, wood,

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.930
or plastic, into a desired
final shape and size.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:27.660
Modern machine shops use
computer-controlled precision

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.510
machining tools for operations
like cutting, drilling, boring,

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:32.100
milling, and so on.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:35.070
Machining is an essential part
of the manufacturing industry.

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:37.830
Historically, a major challenge
of the machining industry

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:41.015
is the time-consuming
task of cost estimation.

00:00:41.015 --> 00:00:42.390
For instance, when
a machine shop

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:44.610
takes an order for
building parts like these,

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:47.430
it needs to determine the
individual cuts and holes that

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:49.520
need to be made for
each individual part

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.510
by carefully reading
the blueprint provided

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:53.020
by the customer.

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:55.020
This manual process
requires machining experts

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:57.722
who are dedicated to the cost
estimation process, which

00:00:57.722 --> 00:01:00.180
can act as a bottleneck for
the productivity of the machine

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:01.440
shop as a whole.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:04.170
A company called Kabuku
in Japan has launched

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:05.880
a new solution
for this challenge

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:08.730
by handling the data management
of their machining process

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:09.870
with AI.

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:12.990
Kabuku is a startup focused on
modernizing the manufacturing

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:15.240
industry with 3D
printing, cloud,

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:18.370
and AI technologies for major
manufacturing customers,

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:21.150
including Toyota,
Honda, and Olympus.

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:24.380
Let's see how Kabuku's
data management tool works.

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:27.240
First, a blueprint is uploaded
to the tool in the web browser,

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:29.760
and a region is
specified for estimation.

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:34.050
Then the user simply presses
the Cost Estimation button.

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:36.150
The tool detects and
highlights every object

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:37.860
that requires processing.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:40.440
You can see the detected
types of processing steps,

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:42.510
how many there are,
how much each costs,

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:45.480
and the total estimated
costs for the entire part.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:48.690
The tool also allows users to
add detailed info for each part

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:52.920
or to have experts update any
part that requires minor fixes.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.260
The tool can detect
tens of processing parts

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:58.170
on the design in less than one
second, which significantly

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:00.450
increases the productivity
of cost estimation

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:03.720
by machining experts.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:07.110
Masahiko Adachi, CEO
of Kabuku, explains

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:08.550
the benefit of this tool.

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:10.259
"If machine shops
can respond quickly

00:02:10.259 --> 00:02:13.120
to cost estimation requests
from their customers,

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:15.330
that's a better customer
experience and more business

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:16.500
opportunities.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:19.170
Additionally, this tool can
act as a central repository

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:21.480
of expert knowledge
for each machine shop.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.550
This allows the shop to
easily share knowledge

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:25.590
with junior staff
members and learners

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:28.410
without any bottlenecks and make
business operations much more

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:29.880
scalable."

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:31.650
Let's learn more
about how Kabuku

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:34.660
built this tool with the
power of Google Cloud AI.

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:37.380
Kabuku's tool was able to
detect the machining operations

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:38.610
from the blueprint.

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:41.940
To achieve this, they used
our AutoML Vision technology

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:43.600
with object detection.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:46.440
First they collected thousands
of images in preparation

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:49.080
for ML model training, with
different labeled blueprints

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:51.720
for drilling, boring, and
cutting operations on them.

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:53.257
Usually, it would
take a lot of time

00:02:53.257 --> 00:02:55.590
to build an object detection
system using their training

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:56.698
data for production use.

00:02:56.698 --> 00:02:58.740
You would need to start
with data pre-processing,

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:01.680
and ML model design,
hyperparameter tuning,

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:04.110
evaluation, and
deployment, and would also

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:07.230
need to have resources to
keep the model up to date.

00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:11.700
And that would require hiring
AI experts and ML engineers.

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:13.590
For faster
time-to-market, Kabuku

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:16.140
chose our AutoML
technology which automates

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:18.720
many steps in the ML lifecycle.

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:20.940
All they had to do was
upload their training images

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:23.760
to AutoML Vision and
press the Train button

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:26.040
to start the automated model
training and development

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:26.540
process.

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:34.930
In half a day, they got
an object detection model

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:37.810
generated by AutoML Vision with
a detailed report of the model

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:40.150
accuracy and various metrics.

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:42.040
Then Kabuku downloaded
the ML model

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:44.110
and used it with
TensorFlow.js, which

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:47.600
allows you to run the object
detection within a web browser.

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:50.470
That's the reason why Kabuku's
machining data management

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:53.830
tool is able to detect tens of
processing parts in just one

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:54.920
second.

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:56.920
Even though you could
build the object detection

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:59.290
model much faster
with AutoML Vision,

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:00.880
that's not the whole story.

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.860
One important requirement
for a Kabuku's tool

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:05.710
is the ability to keep
learning from the experts.

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:07.750
The practices and patterns
used in blueprints

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:10.910
are different for each customer
project or machining expert.

00:04:10.910 --> 00:04:13.840
So the tool provides a UI for
fixing the misdetected parts

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:15.370
or adding more details.

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:16.870
Based on this
feedback from experts,

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:18.730
the tool reruns the
ML training process

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:22.089
and deploys a better ML model
that captures the practices

00:04:22.089 --> 00:04:23.860
and patterns used in each case.

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:29.310
To implement this continuous
ML training process,

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:32.280
Kabuku used Cloud AI
platform pipelines.

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:35.400
This product allows users to
build orchestrated ML pipelines

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:37.710
and manage them from
data pre-processing

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.400
and validation all
the way through

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:42.510
to model training,
validation, and deployment.

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:44.790
Instead of asking AI
experts again and again

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:47.580
for a manual rerun of the
whole training process,

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:49.980
everything can be automated
and continuously integrated

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:53.220
just by invoking the pipeline,
making the whole service robust

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:55.710
and production ready.

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:57.600
With AI platform
pipelines, Kabuku

00:04:57.600 --> 00:04:59.370
was able to build
a positive feedback

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:01.620
loop between the machining
experts and model training

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:04.080
pipeline, resulting in
ever-better accuracy

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:05.760
of their model and
higher productivity

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:07.920
as the experts keep
using the tool.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:10.110
This loop of
application and training

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:13.170
is called active learning in ML.

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:16.410
In summary, Kabuku was able to
use the power of Google Cloud

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:19.290
AI for faster time-to-market,
quick object detection,

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:22.680
and create a flexible ML
pipeline for active learning.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:24.480
What will your AI
journey look like?

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:27.320
Get started today with these
tools from Google Cloud AI.

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:30.370
[MUSIC FADING OUT]

